@startuml app-complete-sequence
' End-to-end flow: GitHub sign-in → AI PR review → bug findings in dashboard
' Verified against backend/src and frontend/src (Code-reviewer).

autonumber

actor "Operator" as Op
participant "React SPA" as SPA
participant "Express API" as API
database "MongoDB" as DB
participant "GitHub" as GH
participant "scripts/pythonExploit.py" as PY

== Sign in with GitHub ==

Op -> SPA : Click Sign in with GitHub
SPA -> API : Browser navigates to\nGET /api/auth/github/start
API -> GH : Redirect to OAuth authorize
Op -> GH : Approve access
GH -> API : GET /api/auth/github/callback?code=
API -> GH : POST oauth/access_token\nthen GET api.github.com/user
API -> DB : Upsert User\n(githubId, email, githubLogin)
API -> SPA : Redirect /auth/finish?token=&next=
SPA -> SPA : Store JWT in localStorage
SPA -> API : GET /api/auth/me\nBearer JWT
API --> SPA : user profile

== Enable automation (order may vary) ==

Op -> SPA : POST /api/keys {name}\non API keys page (session JWT only)
SPA -> API : POST /api/keys\nBearer JWT
API -> DB : Store ApiKey\n(bcrypt hash, prefix)
API --> SPA : Plaintext key once\n(64 hex chars)

Op -> SPA : Paste key on unlock gate
SPA -> API : GET /api/auth/me\nBearer JWT
SPA -> API : GET /api/auth/me\nBearer API key
API -> DB : verifyKey on second call
SPA -> SPA : Store service key\nin localStorage

Op -> SPA : Install GitHub App\non Configurations
SPA -> API : POST /api/github/install-link\nBearer JWT
API --> SPA : GitHub App install URL\n(with state JWT)
SPA -> GH : Browser redirect to install URL
Op -> GH : Select org/user and repositories
GH -> API : Browser GET /api/github/setup\n?installation_id=&state=
API -> DB : Upsert Installation for userId
API -> SPA : Redirect /configurations?installed=1

note over GH, API
  GitHub App webhook must target
  POST /api/webhooks/github
end note

== AI review on pull request ==

Op -> GH : Open or update pull request\n(any author)
GH -> API : POST /api/webhooks/github\npull_request opened | synchronize
API -> API : Verify x-hub-signature-256\n(if GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET set)
API --> GH : 200 Webhook received
API -> DB : Load Installation by installation.id

opt REQUIRE_API_KEY_FOR_REVIEWS=true
  API -> DB : userHasActiveApiKey\nelse skip review
end

API -> DB : Load or upsert RepoConfig\nfor user and repo
API -> GH : Fetch PR diff and changed paths\n(installation Octokit)

loop When diff exceeds segment size
  API -> PY : spawn stdin JSON\n{prompt, diff}
  PY -> PY : HTTPS Gemini stream endpoint
  PY --> API : Review text\n(parseEnforcerResponse bugs JSON)
end

API -> DB : Upsert PrReviewFinding\n(userId, dedupeKey)
API -> API : publish finding-created\nor finding-updated
API -> GH : Post PR review\n(postComment: true, may slim via env)

== Display bugs in dashboard ==

Op -> SPA : Open Bug findings\n(requires unlock gate API key)
SPA -> API : GET /api/findings\nBearer API key or JWT
API -> DB : Query PrReviewFinding\nmatchFindingsVisibleToUser
API --> SPA : {items, total, skip, limit}

SPA -> API : GET /api/findings/by-category\n(same auth)
API -> DB : Aggregate counts by category
API --> SPA : {counts}

SPA -> Op : Render table, filters,\ncategory sidebar

opt Dashboard open with SSE connected
  SPA -> API : EventSource GET /api/events?token=
  API --> SPA : finding-created\nor finding-updated
  SPA -> SPA : Reload findings\nand by-category
end

@enduml
